  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "release",
    "file": "skia/src/gpu/GrGpuResource.cpp",
    "description": "GrGpuResource::release() invokes the virtual onRelease() while the resource is still registered in GrResourceCache, and only removes it from the cache afterward. onRelease() may drop dependent-resource references (notably GrRenderTarget::onRelease clears its stencil attachment) and run a GrSurface release callback, causing reentrant cache/ref-count activity during GrResourceCache::releaseAll(). This permits the shutdown queue to retain stale lifecycle state for the GrMockTextureRenderTarget; CacheAccess::release() then deletes the object, but releaseAll subsequently obtains the freed allocation from the purgeable queue and calls GrGpuResource::release() again, producing the UAF at line 52. The vulnerable ordering is in GrGpuResource::release(), rather than the final read itself.",
    "conditions": "The fuzz data must drive the mock Ganesh canvas into creating a renderable mock texture (GrMockTextureRenderTarget) together with resource dependencies/callback-driven cache activity such as a stencil attachment, and leave the resources purgeable until GrContextFactory destroys the GrDirectContext. During GrResourceCache::releaseAll(), releasing that render target executes its onRelease chain while it is still cache-visible; the resulting reentrant resource unrefs/cache mutations leave a stale entry that is processed after CacheAccess::release has deleted the target. The supplied PoV reaches this state during context teardown; no direct attacker pointer control is required."
  },
